Well, the firmware loading logic has been flaky on my system for a few=20
releases now. I previously reported bug 527265 against 2.6.29, where the=20
qla1040 firmware would not load at all, and that was resolved in a later=20
2.6.29 image.

In this release (2.6.30-2) I get new/different bad behavior. My system=20
has three QLA1040 cards in it. In the attached console output from the boot=
,=20
notice that at time 23.256824, the first adapter (scsi0) is located,=20
generates a stack trace trying to load firmware, and fails to initialize=20
the card. (There goes my tape drive!) A little later, at 83.499957, the=20
second adapter is found and this time the firmware loads fine. Ditto for=20
the third adapter after that.

